1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,200
Morning starts with a lamp check.

2
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:04,000
Sounds like a metaphor. It's a job.

3
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:05,700
The hearth has to be lit before anything else counts.

4
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:06,900
One breath, and the coals remember.

5
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:09,400
Then the stones. Visitors leave them on the shelf.

6
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:11,700
A name, a note, sometimes just a coal.

7
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:14,000
I read every one.

8
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:16,400
Somebody noticed. Apparently, that's the whole job.

9
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:19,000
Warden rounds. The quiet ones don't say when they're running low.

10
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:21,300
So you learn to listen. Check in, leave the door open, don't make it weird.

11
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:23,600
Then the songs. Embers in, songs out.

12
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:27,200
Evening, the chairs come out.

13
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:29,300
The flames are the opening act. The element is the part after.

14
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:31,600
When the smoke drifts somewhere worth drifting and everybody's still sitting.

15
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:34,900
Keep the lamp lit. Read the stones. Feed the fire.
